# Double-safety net for `npm pack`. The `files` field in package.json is
# the primary allowlist; this file is a defence-in-depth deny list so
# that an accidental `files` field edit (e.g. switching to a glob like
# `lib/**` instead of `lib/**/*.js`) does NOT silently ship the wrong
# payload to the marketplace.
#
# Precedence (npm): anything matched by `package.json#files` CANNOT be
# excluded from here — `files` wins. So these rules only bite when a path
# is NOT already named in `files`, and they can never subtract from a path
# that is. Do not list a path under both: the deny line is a silent no-op
# and it makes this file look stricter than it is.

# Source — never published; lib/ holds the compiled output.
src/

# Tests + fixtures — never published.
tests/

# Local install artifacts and build outputs that are NOT meant for npm.
# NOTE: `lib/` is deliberately absent — `files` allowlists `lib/**/*.js`
# and `lib/types/**/*.d.ts`, and `files` overrides this file, so a `lib/`
# line here would be inert while implying the opposite. Source maps stay
# excluded by the `**/*.js.map` rule at the bottom.
install/
tsconfig.json
tsconfig.client.tsbuildinfo
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
vitest.config.ts
.github/
.gitlab-ci.yml

# Local-only helper scripts and dev-time verification scripts.
# The release-facing scripts (inspect-events / check-readme-sync /
# stress-spl-interactive) are explicitly listed in package.json#files, so
# they are NOT excluded here. Everything else in scripts/ (prepare /
# build-client / verify-*) is developer-only.
scripts/build-client.mjs
scripts/prepare.mjs
scripts/formalName.mjs
scripts/eval-spl-accuracy-fp.mjs
scripts/spl-eval-corpus.mjs
scripts/verify-artifacts.mjs
scripts/verify-self-contained.mjs
scripts/verify-spl-block-code-detector.mjs
scripts/verify-test-cases-coverage.mjs

# Claude Code / AI-agent local state.
.claude/
.ccgui/
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md

# Build-tool / lockfile noise that is not the published artefact.
node_modules/
*.log
*.tgz
pnpm-lock.yaml
package-lock.json

# Source maps — never ship. They disclose `src/` paths to the
# consumer. If a stack trace is needed in production, upload to a
# service (Sentry / source-map-uploader) out of band.
**/*.js.map
**/*.d.ts.map
**/*.mjs.map
